#title: B-scan from a metal cylinder in some sand or air


@@ General Setup @@
/#domain: 4.0 2.0 1.0
#domain: 3.0 2.0 1.0
This^ is the bounds of the sim in meters.

#dx_dy_dz: 0.02 0.02 0.02
^Discrete chunks of the sim, also in meters

/#time_window: 30e-9
#time_window: 20e-9
In seconds of the sim^


@@ Materials @@
/#material: 3 0.01 1 0 my_sand
/#material: 1 0 1 0 air 
/#material: 6 .10 1 0 wet_asphalt
/#material: 6 0 1 0 half_space
^epsilon, conductivity, mu, magnetic loss, name

@@ Shapes @@
/#box: 0 0 0 3 2 1 my_sand
/#box: 0 0 0 3 2 1 air
#box: 0 0 0 3 2 1 free_space
/#box: 0 0 0 2 2 1 my_sand
^adjusted smaller box
Makes a box of a specified material^

/#sphere: 1.125 1.375 0.75 0.25 pec n
Makes a sphere at ^ with radius of .25m of 
a Perfect Electric Conductor and no dielectric smoothing

/#cylinder: 1.250 1.000 0.200 1.250 1.000 0.700 0.500 pec n


@@ Diff distance cylinders to test linear relationship @@
% #cylinder: 0.250 1.000 0.200 0.250 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^2m??? (seems too far)
#cylinder: 1.250 1.000 0.200 1.250 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^1m
% #cylinder: 1.650 1.000 0.200 1.650 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^0.5m
/#cylinder: 1.800 1.000 0.200 1.800 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^0.25m

^half a meter attempt to see if distance attenuates too much. Inital try at .8 - 1.2 for step size of 0.04
/#cylinder: 1.125 2.325 0.1 1.125 2.375 0.8 0.50 wet_asphalt n
^REMEMBER any time you change radius, reposition so still 1m away or chosen distance


@@ EM Wave stuff @@
#waveform: ricker 1 6e8 my_pulse
/#waveform: ricker 50 6e8 my_pulse
^What happens if A=1 increased to 5? Nothing. Even if bumped up to 50, no difference!

/#hertzian_dipole: z 2.300 0.800 0.500 my_pulse     
#hertzian_dipole: z 2.300 0.900 0.500 my_pulse     

/#rx: 2.300 0.600 0.500                               
#rx: 2.300 0.700 0.500                               

% % %
When running dif iteration numbers, run rx and tx at different positions to recenter
i.e. 10 iter start 0.5 to 1.5 (so 0.4rx and 0.6tx), 20 iter had to drop stepsize to 0.05 and ran from same location
and for og, start 0.8 to 1.2 (so rx: 0.7 and tx: 0.9) with 0.1 stepsize
% % %

#src_steps: 0 0.1 0
#rx_steps: 0 0.1 0
% % % let's try doing 10 steps at 0.1m stepsize
Max_iters = 50, so optimal is lowest spacing of 2, then scale up for even spacing between start and end, which should be ...? 16 again? and this is not even max, because you
could go all the way and start at .4 and .6 and end at 1.4 and 1.6 
% % %


/#geometry_view: 0 0 0 3 2 1 0.02 0.02 0.02 big_bscan_test n
^adjusted for new 1m smaller domain in x direc
^position, discretization, filename, and normal not fine so smaller filesize



To run paraview go in terminal while in gprMax env, and go to ~/Downloads/Paraview..../bin and then use command ./paraview to open it. open another terminal if want to keep using paraview, or close and reopen after changes have been made

To run -n 5 times and get the scan:
python -m gprMax ascan_1m_cyl_bscan.in -n 5
python -m tools.outputfiles_merge ascan_1m_cyl_bscan --remove-files
python -m tools.plot_Bscan ascan_1m_cyl_bscan_merged.out Ez
